---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "@/components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { getMessages } from "@/lib/i18n";
import { homePath, newsIndexPath } from "@/lib/locale";

const lang = "en" as const;
const t = getMessages(lang);
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  path="/404/"
  title="When Is A Page Found? — fotonoza"
  description="A mildly philosophical 404 page about searching, finding, and where photos wait."
  alternatePaths={{ en: homePath("en"), pl: homePath("pl") }}
>
  <SiteHeader
    lang={lang}
    homeHref={homePath(lang)}
    newsHref={newsIndexPath(lang)}
    switchHref={homePath("pl")}
    switchLabel="🇵🇱 PL"
    t={t}
  />

  <article class="container py-16">
    <header class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">
        <a
          href={newsIndexPath(lang)}
          class="text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-yellow-300 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-yellow-300/80 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-zinc-950"
        >
          ← News
        </a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-zinc-600">·</span>
        <a
          href={homePath(lang)}
          class="text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-yellow-300 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-yellow-300/80 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-zinc-950"
        >
          fotonoza
        </a>
      </p>
      <time class="mt-4 block text-sm text-zinc-500">404</time>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
        If a page is missing, were we looking for the page, or for the feeling of being certain?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-zinc-400">
        A brief field note from the border between maps and territory.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-6 leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
      <p>
        Photographers learn this early: the frame is never the world, only a decision about where to stop the world.
        A missing page behaves the same way. You clicked with confidence, expecting arrival, and instead found a soft
        interruption. Not an error in your intelligence; just a reminder that paths are stories we tell ourselves until
        infrastructure disagrees.
      </p>
      <p>
        Maybe this page is absent. Maybe it stepped outside for coffee. Maybe it existed for one commit, one deploy, one
        perfect minute, and now lives only as a rumor in browser history. We call that broken, but photographs call it
        timing: a thing was there, then light moved on.
      </p>
      <p>
        So if you came here searching for certainty, consider this a better gift: orientation. You still have the lens,
        the road back to home, and the right to ask where to point next. In editing and in wandering, progress rarely means
        never missing. It means noticing quickly, smiling anyway, and taking the next deliberate step.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 pt-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-3">
          <img
            src="/browse.png"
            alt="Photorealistic conceptual scene for the 404 page."
            width={1280}
            height={720}
            class="h-auto w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-500">Photorealistic concept slot (temporary).</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-3">
          <img
            src="/adjust.png"
            alt="Comic style conceptual scene for the 404 page."
            width={1280}
            height={720}
            class="h-auto w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-zinc-500">Comic-style concept slot (temporary).</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
